From b0645568f96e7d98989d3802c2a2aad5f5571ff2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alec Stewat <me@alec-stewart.dev>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 21:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] switch default cc to clang

Chimera's bldroot only ships clang, not gcc. Nim's stock config
hardcodes `cc = gcc`, so every `bin/nim c` invocation falls over with
`/bin/sh: gcc: not found` once we're past the C bootstrap (which
already picks up clang via cbuild's tool resolution).

`compiler clang:` is a first-class backend in extccomp.nim, so this is
a one-line swap. Affects koch boot, koch tools, and any direct
`bin/nim c` calls we make.

diff --git a/config/nim.cfg b/config/nim.cfg
index 038c3c9..c20aada 100644
--- a/config/nim.cfg
+++ b/config/nim.cfg
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@
 # Environment variables can be accessed like so:
 #  gcc.path %= "$CC_PATH"
 
-cc = gcc
+cc = clang
 
 # additional options always passed to the compiler:
 --parallel_build: "0" # 0 to auto-detect number of processors
--
2.0
